#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204092 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203854 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "36eadc0b-c2b0-5f84-8f39-2b8399932edb" :question/math-academy-id "e-17214" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2nx + 7  = -4x + 5\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $n?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ax = b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $4x$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2nx+7 & =-4x+5 \\\\ 2nx+4x+7 & =-4x+5+4x \\\\ 2nx+4x+7 & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $7$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2nx+4x+7 & =5 \\\\ 2nx+4x+7-7 & =5-7 \\\\ 2nx+4x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $x$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(2n + 4)x  = -2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(2n + 4)}_{a}x  = \\underbrace{-2}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2n + 4= 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $n,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n+4 & =0 \\\\ 2n+4-4 & =0-4 \\\\ 2n & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{2n}{2} & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\ n & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051079}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0f08b77-eeef-5fc2-8543-09a2276b46e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203498} {:answer/id #uuid "ed88b415-ec31-5753-9538-94d29a0edac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203499} {:answer/id #uuid "06e406e9-458f-5b5b-8a76-47ae321cb09d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203500} {:answer/id #uuid "217b4c73-d235-5933-8a9f-ef748ad498ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203501} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc66499-02a0-5560-9357-f491dc4ae661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203502}] :answer-field/id #uuid "204618ec-8108-58ed-8408-6f51fe3d50c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203497}] :question/id #uuid "c5eb239a-6da7-5d84-946d-c53824d57aa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-287677" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x$, given by\n$2px = 3x + 5$\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "41d7cf18-e5fd-5caa-873f-517786f6a348" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203503}] :question/id #uuid "13915c55-7c7c-53b4-adee-86cf0ce79ae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-287678" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x$, given by\n$2px + 6 = 4x + 5$\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p$?$p =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae663b6-85c5-5077-b87c-a6180d34333b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295510} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4fa932-686f-5272-80f1-319a4616fc55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295695} {:answer/id #uuid "5513a93f-ae93-5de6-bdce-765af89d5be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295759} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfab9aa-d797-5176-8659-fc606759afe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296346} {:answer/id #uuid "f950fb0f-6b6e-53ca-bbe7-61f27fce1157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdfab9aa-d797-5176-8659-fc606759afe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296346} :answer-field/id #uuid "1839f0af-c2f8-56ec-a3e2-a0f1a0ec6286" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6cf4ece6-fb8b-5a6f-963d-f97832f4331b" :question/math-academy-id "q-288662" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n3py=5y+8\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ay=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $5y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3py & =5y+8 \\\\ 3py-5y & =5y+8-5y \\\\ 3py-5y & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $y$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(3p-5)y=8.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ay=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(3p-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}y={{8}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3p-5=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-5 & =0 \\\\ 3p-5+5 & =0+5 \\\\ 3p & =5 \\\\ \\frac{3p}{3} & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9acb3749-840c-51ad-9eb4-ee8c920e6230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9acb3749-840c-51ad-9eb4-ee8c920e6230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296092} :answer-field/id #uuid "31011122-f1db-5927-9c5b-95335e1dd8b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa4e94a9-eff0-5fbb-b2d3-1dcbd9a3e5ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-288673" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n3qz+4=7z+1\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $az=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $7z$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3qz+4 & =7z+1 \\\\ 3qz-7z+4 & =7z+1-7z \\\\ 3qz-7z+4 & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $4$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3qz-7z+4 & =1 \\\\ 3qz-7z+4-4 & =1-4 \\\\ 3qz-7z & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $z$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(3q-7)z=-3.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $az=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(3q-7)}_{⏟}}_{a}z={{-3}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3q-7=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3q-7 & =0 \\\\ 3q-7+7 & =0+7 \\\\ 3q & =7 \\\\ \\frac{3q}{3} & =\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ q & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03a617fe-2ec0-59b8-aa7e-a8f0c47af481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03a617fe-2ec0-59b8-aa7e-a8f0c47af481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295282} :answer-field/id #uuid "52022133-680b-5a4f-b274-743fc5a96fa9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9c5e8ea4-ee94-5a1f-a3c1-cf0a3b495462" :question/math-academy-id "q-288674" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $u,$ given by\n\n$$\n5ru+3=2u+6\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $au=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $2u$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ru+3 & =2u+6 \\\\ 5ru-2u+3 & =2u+6-2u \\\\ 5ru-2u+3 & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $3$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5ru-2u+3 & =6 \\\\ 5ru-2u+3-3 & =6-3 \\\\ 5ru-2u & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $u$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(5r-2)u=3.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $au=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(5r-2)}_{⏟}}_{a}u={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n5r-2=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5r-2 & =0 \\\\ 5r-2+2 & =0+2 \\\\ 5r & =2 \\\\ \\frac{5r}{5} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ r & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d96f33ba-5b23-51ab-944b-35f7ed28804d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d96f33ba-5b23-51ab-944b-35f7ed28804d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296414} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb1883d7-5f64-5b1c-9d6c-398589b85515" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "169f6fd4-529f-5b4e-9fcd-e754c540805a" :question/math-academy-id "q-288675" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $w,$ given by\n\n$$\n-4mw+5=-3w+1\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $m?$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $aw=b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $3w$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4mw+5 & =-3w+1 \\\\ -4mw+3w+5 & =-3w+1+3w \\\\ -4mw+3w+5 & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $5$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4mw+3w+5 & =1 \\\\ -4mw+3w+5-5 & =1-5 \\\\ -4mw+3w & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $w$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(-4m+3)w=-4.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $aw=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(-4m+3)}_{⏟}}_{a}w={{-4}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-4m+3=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4m+3 & =0 \\\\ -4m+3-3 & =0-3 \\\\ -4m & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{-4m}{-4} & =\\frac{-3}{-4} \\\\ m & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38f1f5d0-a65b-50e5-ae53-71603b6a4f59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38f1f5d0-a65b-50e5-ae53-71603b6a4f59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295592} :answer-field/id #uuid "0392835c-e04b-5ad0-8c8d-d5dc8f5281c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93ece185-5396-5f04-8ab8-086b4b609861" :question/math-academy-id "q-288678" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n-3pz-8=-z-6\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $az=b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $z$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz-8 & =-z-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-z-6+z \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we add $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz+z-8 & =-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8+8 & =-6+8 \\\\ -3pz+z & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $z$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(-3p+1)z=2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(-3p+1)}_{⏟}}_{a}z={{2}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-3p+1=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3p+1 & =0 \\\\ -3p+1-1 & =0-1 \\\\ -3p & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{-3p}{-3} & =\\frac{-1}{-3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}]}
